invariant: INV-35
file: build.h
catches: test/lib-check-webpki-record.sh
reason: CH_BUILD_AXES leaves out the CH_TRANSPORT_TCP_NONBLOCKING term. The object
  and every consumer compute the axes from the same header, so the two
  still agree and a comparison between them cannot see it: a
  tcp-nonblocking object and a tcp-blocking one now differ in no bit. test/build_test.c
  restates the axes from its own defines, one line per define, and exits
  2 when CH_BUILD_AXES disagrees with them, so lib-check objects.

--- old
     CH_BUILD_IF_TRANSPORT_TCP_NONBLOCKING | CH_BUILD_IF_SUITE_AES_GCM | CH_BUILD_IF_ROLE_SERVER | \
--- new
     CH_BUILD_IF_SUITE_AES_GCM | CH_BUILD_IF_ROLE_SERVER | \
